iOS 27.2 expands Multiview to the iPhone, so users can watch up to four live sports streams simultaneously.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/Apple-Sports-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1035086" /><br/>
Multiview works for sports events included in an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> subscription: Major League Soccer (MLS), Formula 1 (F1) in the U.S., and Friday Night Baseball doubleheaders during the Major League Baseball season.<br/>
<br/>
With Formula 1, users can select a preset team Multiview for live events, or build their own from multiple F1 feeds like onboard cameras and track maps.<br/>
<br/>
